  "entry": "code/home.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Filter the bundled seawater isotope and hydrographic compilations (EnvGeo ECS–Japan Sea, Around Japan, Global) by region, transect, reference, time, depth and value ranges, then view them as T-S diagrams, depth profiles, salinity–δ18O regressions, maps and 3D/4D scatters, optionally with your own uploaded measurements and a check for duplicates across datasets. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
